  Status: draft; the revised source correspondence is submitted for
  independent review. This unit proves the shell-specific composition
  conditional on the selected same-history service, price, and quota
  receipts; it does not claim to close the full stress construction.

  <section|Source pin and scope><label|source-pin-and-scope>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Vendored Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Claim: #26, in the isolated clone
    <verbatim|/private/tmp/ym-existence-lattice-20261111>.

    <item>Only outputs owned here: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-stress-shell-nodes.tex>
    and <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/actual-stress-shell-nodes-evidence.md>.

    <item>No Lean source, shared manuscript, or metadata was edited.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source crosswalk><label|source-crosswalk>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  item in the draft>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified
  declaration>>|<cell|<strong|Source path>>|<cell|<strong|What the source
  establishes / boundary>>>|<row|<cell|Same-family public route and actual
  Aroma input>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/RG17/Joint.lean>>|<cell|From
  the retained run records, builds <verbatim|Created C>, then <verbatim|Aroma
  C> using <verbatim|laurelE> and <verbatim|fugacious>; then passes that same
  Aroma into <verbatim|readyA>. This is the public route inspected, not an
  alternate family or history.>>|<row|<cell|Economic schedule and shell-node
  conclusion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.Economics>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.laurelE>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fugacious>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Economist.lean>>|<cell|Chooses
  <verbatim|t=1+1/(64(d+12))>, a mesh subsequence with scale ratio tending to
  t, and invokes <verbatim|pricey>, <verbatim|lightness>, room and
  <verbatim|bricks> for each fixed opening, labels, and finite extraction
  order. <verbatim|fugacious> supplies the scale note for
  <verbatim|fuga(i+1)>.>>|<row|<cell|Paid shell-node numerical
  gates>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.pricey>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.lightness>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.pitts>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Burrough.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|pricey>
  gives positive product <verbatim|ventola>, the marched price
  <verbatim|\<leq\>\<delta\>_i ventola/(16 bling_i)>, and
  <verbatim|32(1+columns_i)pitts_i\<\|\|\>alto(k,D)\<\|\|\>(e_i/gainChart(i,k))\<leq\>fly(D,k)/2>;
  its strict rate is <verbatim|(d+12)(1\<minus\>t)\<gtr\>\<minus\>1/32>.
  <verbatim|lightness> gives <verbatim|32 fuga(i+1)\<leq\>a_p> and
  <verbatim|a_{i+1}(B_{i+1}\<twosuperior\>+1+2
  polls_{i+1})\<leq\>a_p>.>>|<row|<cell|Exact two-channel price
  definitions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.picket>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.ventola>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.scurry>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Brick.lean>>|<cell|The
  two factors use Bool false/true as insertion-channel labels.
  <verbatim|picket> calls <verbatim|ventola> at <verbatim|i=m+1>; both outer
  and inner scalar factors are therefore <verbatim|renal(m+1)>, so the
  numerator is <verbatim|delta_(m+1)^2>, with the further input
  <verbatim|near(j)>. The grade-four insertion price is divided by
  <verbatim|fuga(i+1)^h>. <verbatim|scurry> uses the distinct fine occupancy
  <verbatim|r(i+1)>; its geometric stencil radius is <verbatim|polls=1024
  B^2>, while the exponential count is <verbatim|peepers=(2\<centerdot\>1024
  B+1)^4>. <verbatim|krill(j,i,b)=b/16(a_j/a_i)^4> is defined in
  <verbatim|North/Ossola.lean>.>>|<row|<cell|Local root and quota output at
  each anchor>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.Wares>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.sales>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.bricks>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.faraway>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Siroco.lean>,
  <verbatim|North/Brim.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Wares> carries the Thor
  controls, Runs and Throws at all levels. <verbatim|sales> returns a grade-D
  label with quota <verbatim|\<leq\>2e>, chamber membership and root test
  <verbatim|\<leq\>2 stakes/c>. <verbatim|bricks> obtains this for each fixed
  collar cover point after eventual placement, near-center and room
  conditions. It uses the exact fragment <verbatim|(fuga(m+1))^h
  O(T,location)O(B,0)\<minus\>O(z,0)>. The late filter is pointwise in the
  anchor; the numerical bound is common.>>|<row|<cell|Finite two-channel
  assembly>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.mutation>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.bequeathed>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Brick.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/South/Merman.lean>>|<cell|Caps the two channel
  sources, uses maximizing/placement geometry, then calls the coefficient
  construction, bridge and <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.bequeathed>; the exact
  output is the <verbatim|sales> root/quota bound
  <verbatim|2\<centerdot\>stakes/c>. For the final factor 2,
  <verbatim|bequeathed> writes the root-tested difference as
  <verbatim|(f+r')+(-r'-O(B,0))>; with <verbatim|S=stakes/w> (here
  <verbatim|w=c_m>), the first summand is bounded by <verbatim|S>, the second
  by <verbatim|S/2> and hence by <verbatim|S>. The triangle inequality for
  the root seminorm gives <verbatim|2S=2\<centerdot\>stakes/c_m>. The factor
  does not come from combining regular and forced coefficient
  charges.>>|<row|<cell|One-step coefficient
  ledger>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.sail>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Arco.lean>>|<cell|Produces
  <verbatim|Q\<#2080\>> with order-zero format, remainder bound,
  coefficient-size <verbatim|\<leq\>a_{m+1}^D x(4/A)>, and <verbatim|Served>
  identity for the pushed two-channel birth. These four fields are stated in
  ordinary mathematical terms in the manuscript.>>|<row|<cell|Root-test
  copies and reflection>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Cells.Tiling.copy>,
  <verbatim|YM.Cells.Tiling.rootTest>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/Tiling.lean>>|<cell|The
  finite product is over <verbatim|T.Cell> for the centered chamber tiling at
  the opened reference level; each copy pulls back under its prescribed
  motion/translation and is complex-conjugated for odd reflection parity. The
  root is the cell-count root of the normalized moment, not a product over
  all fine sites.>>|<row|<cell|Fine response
  construction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.upper>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Flank.lean>>|<cell|Uses
  the Geyser/Thor response inputs, migrated sites, occupancy, separation,
  response-cost bounds, and same-history factorization of each insertion. It
  constructs a response certificate at level j.>>|<row|<cell|Response
  transport from j to m+1>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.ossuary>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Ossola.lean>>|<cell|Backward-transports
  the response. The proof uses <verbatim|krill(j,i,b)=b/16(a_j/a_i)^4>;
  adjacent block ratio L\<geqslant\>2 gives fourth-power amplification and
  <verbatim|6L\<leq\>L\<#2074\>>; it propagates occupancy, separation, and
  the endpoint weighted response.>>|<row|<cell|Two-channel graft and
  coefficient extraction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.dusks>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.grafted>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fuseNext>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Dolphin.lean>,
  <verbatim|North/Anise.lean>, <verbatim|North/Lamplit.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|dusks>
  combines false/true channels, checks zero-anchor/affine covariance, then
  calls <verbatim|grafted> and <verbatim|fuseNext>; <verbatim|fuseNext>
  obtains the finite coupon from <verbatim|tossing>, applies the one-step
  <verbatim|Duty.pre> conversion, and returns the coefficient
  ledger.>>|<row|<cell|Exact one-step menu condition and price
  arithmetic>|<cell|YM.MergeProof.Accent.Duty, YM.MergeProof.Accent.Duty.pre,
  YM.MergeProof.Menu.Volant, YM.MergeProof.Menu.stroke>|<cell|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Temper.lean,
  Copse.lean, Menu.lean>|<cell|Duty.pre consumes the selected menu offer and
  tariff; Menu.stroke is its served-transfer step. The selected paid menu and
  same-history specialization are proved in the canonical parent units listed
  below.>>|<row|<cell|Quota-to-label norm
  conversion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.quota>,
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.quota_stop>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Least.lean>>|<cell|The
  quota is <verbatim|quota C D m N p z>: its second index is the moving birth
  level <verbatim|m>, not the opening. <verbatim|Brim.bricks> applies the
  quota stop at <verbatim|m>, using <verbatim|ref(D)\<leq\>k\<leq\>m>. Thus
  its finite norm constant can depend on <verbatim|m>; there is no source
  receipt for one constant uniform in birth level. For each fixed
  <verbatim|m>, it is independent of volume and period. The opening
  <verbatim|p0> selects the root-test chamber and stake bound, not the quota
  index.>>|<row|<cell|Exact regular/forced density
  form>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.Served>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.restore>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.Carton>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.Towed>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.field>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.grid>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Domino.radiant>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Domino.sunny>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Accent.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Domino.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|restore> is
  exactly action exponential times <verbatim|Poly.pass(Mach \<Phi\> +
  \<Sigma\> H)> times the box field. <verbatim|Poly.pass> is the finite sum
  <verbatim|\<Sigma\>_{r=0}^{\|I\|} Z^r/r!>. <verbatim|field> sums only
  patterns whose full box supports are pairwise disjoint and whose flags
  union to the target flags. The <verbatim|Carton> and <verbatim|Towed>
  fields give support, no-degree-0/1, and separate summable regular/forced
  cost bounds; these residual terms are not a single coefficient
  readout.>>|<row|<cell|Rate, scale, and normalization
  definitions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fuga>, <verbatim|polls>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.whims>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.plumR>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.gainChart>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.alto>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fly>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.pica>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.quilled>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.seeing>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Vert.lean>,
  <verbatim|Sultan.lean>, <verbatim|Traps.lean>, <verbatim|Cashew.lean>,
  <verbatim|Bid/Loan.lean>, <verbatim|Stove.lean>, <verbatim|Wicker.lean>,
  <verbatim|Welch.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|fuga(i)=128 B_i\<twosuperior\>a_i>;
  <verbatim|whims> uses the two channel label sizes and divides the
  grade-four branch by <verbatim|fuga(m+1)^h>; <verbatim|alto> has norm
  <verbatim|a_k^{-D}>; gain is <verbatim|exp((scale(i)\<minus\>scale(k))/8)>;
  <verbatim|fly> is the inverse winter power of effective coupling.
  <verbatim|quilled> gives the exact channel product rate
  <verbatim|\<minus\>D+(d+12)(1\<minus\>t)>. The column count is rate zero.
  This yields correction-price rate <verbatim|1/32\<minus\>M\<minus\>1/8=\<minus\>5/64>;
  the marched-price comparison uses the explicit growth bound and has rate
  gap <verbatim|\<minus\>61/64>.>>>>>

  <section|Canonical prose reused><label|canonical-prose-reused>

  The parent manuscript now supplies prose proofs for the menu and transfer
  receipts used by this unit. I read these parent files read-only and matched
  their exact assumptions:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>manuscript/existence/rg-multisource.tex, Section
    sec:ex-lattice-rg-multisource: selected paid terms, local menu jet,
    per-box quiet/singleton identities, and the pushed expression.

    <item>manuscript/existence/rg-construction.tex, Theorem
    thm:ex-lattice-volant-supplier and subsection
    subsec:ex-lattice-volant-producer: rooted tariff conversion and grouping
    of the already-paid ungrouped rows.

    <item>manuscript/existence/finite-menu-history-handoff.tex, Section
    sec:finite-menu-history-handoff: same adjacent-scale history, door,
    support exponents, tariff inputs, and explicit Duty specialization.

    <item>manuscript/existence/local-transfer.tex, Section
    sec:local-transfer: the mathematical content of Duty.pre/Menu.stroke,
    including the finite served-transfer calculation.

    <item>manuscript/existence/centered-public-service.tex, Theorem
    thm:ex-selected-run-service, and selected-centered-service.tex, Section
    sec:selected-centered-service: selected public service and endpoint
    support-exponent bounds.
  </itemize-minus>

  Thus this shell unit does not re-prove those canonical estimates. It
  translates the remaining shell chain upper -\<gtr\> ossuary -\<gtr\> dusks
  -\<gtr\> fuseNext/sail, then derives the collar location, quota-to-label
  norm, and root estimate. The exact numerical gate is stated in the
  manuscript and matched to the cited same-history Duty specialization.

  <section|Mathematical distinctions retained><label|mathematical-distinctions-retained>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>The root functional uses the cell-copy set of the centered chamber
    tiling for the opened reference level <verbatim|p0>, as in
    <verbatim|YM.Cells.Tiling.rootTest>; it is not an average over the entire
    fine torus. Each tiling copy includes its translation and the source's
    odd-reflection complex conjugation.

    <item><verbatim|fuga(m+1)> is the physical annulus scale in the fragment;
    it is not the fine mesh <verbatim|a_{m+1}>.

    <item>The price <verbatim|c_m=exp(scale(m)/32)> diverges because
    <verbatim|scale(m)=log(a_m^{-1})\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>>;
    <verbatim|a_m\<rightarrow\>0>.

    <item>The finite coefficient output is not only a size estimate: its
    <verbatim|Format>, remainder, and <verbatim|Served> density identity are
    all needed for the later bridge.

    <item>The two-channel product is handled by the finite mutation/served
    construction, not by an unproved submultiplicativity claim for the
    normalized root functional.

    <item>The source quantifier is: for every fixed collar anchor, the
    relevant volume-period event is late; common numeric estimates do not
    imply one common late event for the whole growing collar.

    <item>The Ribbons.bricks result supplies the fragment and correction at
    each fixed anchor. The shell manuscript then translates the continuation
    through Ribbons.sail, including the coefficient ledger, same-history
    served identity, and pointwise late-set quantifier. The selected menu and
    transfer assumptions are tied to the reviewed parent prose units listed
    above.
  </itemize-minus>

