  <section|Rate and density details added in the repaired
  draft><label|rate-and-density-details-added-in-the-repaired-draft>

  The repaired manuscript gives the paid width explicitly. With (g_q) the
  maximal engineering degree at grade (q), its positive price is

  <\equation*>
    w<rsub|q><around|(|v,j|)>=<frac|<wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|j><rsup|-<around|(|g<rsub|q>+4|)>>|v*C<rsub|j>*<big|prod><rsub|\<ell\>\<less\>j>C<rsub|\<ell\>+1>>.
  </equation*>

  This is the ordinary-mathematical restatement of <verbatim|plumR> and
  <verbatim|Mix.width>: <verbatim|plumR> multiplies (a_j^q) by the width at
  power (2,\\mathrm{winter}(G,q)), <verbatim|hatCoupling> is
  <math|<wide|\<beta\>|^><rsup|-1/2>>, and <verbatim|Mix.envelope> is the
  label price times the current column count and the product of preceding
  column counts. The grade-four branch has the further factor (r_m^{-h}).

  The rate proof uses the exact channel factors, with both renal factors at
  <verbatim|m+1> (because the source evaluates the menu at <verbatim|i=m+1>):

  <\equation*>
    \<rho\><rsub|m,->:-d*t+4*<around|(|1-t|)>,<space|2em>\<rho\><rsub|m,+>:-4*t+h+4*<around|(|1-t|)>,
  </equation*>

  so their product rate is (h+8-(d+12)t=-D+(d+12)(1-t)). The price error rate
  is (1/32-M-1/8=-5/64), and the marched price comparison has rate gap
  (1/32-1-M=-61/64), with (M=-1/64). These are ordinary rate calculations
  spelled out in TeX; the source lemmas <verbatim|pica>, <verbatim|quilled>,
  and <verbatim|seeing> establish the per-factor rate/growth receipts under
  the selected-history hypotheses. The proof also records the subexponential
  column product from the cumulative column-rate receipt, not only the
  current column count.

  The quota itself is indexed by birth level, <verbatim|quota C D m N p z>,
  and the quota constant is birth-level dependent: the source applies
  <verbatim|quota_stop> with <verbatim|ref(D)\<leq\>k\<leq\>m>. It yields a
  finite (Q_m^{\\mathrm{quota}}) at each fixed (m), uniform in volume and
  period, not a constant uniform over all birth levels. The marched estimate
  uses <verbatim|fly(D,m)\<leq\>1>; the source inequality <verbatim|(s_i+1/2)
  peepers_i \<leq\> sqrt(betaHat_(i+1))> makes the exponential channel
  denominator rate zero. The strict lower bound
  <verbatim|M\<gtr\>\<minus\>1/32> is sufficient for the correction-price
  decay, not asserted sharp. Fine response/graft occupancy is (r(m+1));
  served transfer occupancy is (r(m)).

  The displayed density identity unpacks <verbatim|Accent.Served> and
  <verbatim|Accent.restore>: regular coefficients indexed by supports and
  forced coefficients indexed by boxes remain as higher-degree terms.
  <verbatim|Accent.field> sums full-support- disjoint box families whose
  flags cover the target. The manuscript does not replace this identity by a
  single leading coefficient.

  Additional targeted source reads during this repair:

  <\verbatim-code>
    rg -n 'def Served\|structure Carton\|def Towed\|def restore\|def
    field\|def grid' Lean/YM/MergeProof/Accent.lean

    sed -n '1,85p' Lean/YM/MergeProof/Accent.lean

    rg -n 'def radiant\|def sunny' Lean/YM/MergeProof/Domino.lean

    sed -n '1,55p' Lean/YM/MergeProof/Domino.lean

    sed -n '1,100p' Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Wings.lean

    sed -n '1,100p' Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Wicker.lean

    sed -n '1,90p' Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Welch.lean

    sed -n '1,80p' Lean/YM/Work/I04.lean
  </verbatim-code>

  I also inspected <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Brick.lean>,
  <verbatim|Sultan.lean>, <verbatim|Stove.lean>, and <verbatim|Traps.lean>
  for the exact channel indexing and width normalization. No TeX or Lean
  build was run.

